---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import LegalHeader from "../components/legal/LegalHeader.astro";
import GuideNav from "../components/help/GuideNav.astro";
import Callout from "../components/help/Callout.astro";

const sections = [
  { id: "about", label: "About these terms" },
  { id: "accounts", label: "Your account" },
  { id: "using", label: "Using NyasaBuy" },
  { id: "listings", label: "Listings" },
  { id: "buying", label: "Buying" },
  { id: "selling", label: "Selling" },
  { id: "payments", label: "Payments and fees" },
  { id: "delivery", label: "Delivery and confirmation" },
  { id: "disputes", label: "Problems and refunds" },
  { id: "boosts", label: "Featured listings" },
  { id: "chat", label: "Chat and conduct" },
  { id: "prohibited", label: "Not allowed" },
  { id: "content", label: "Your content" },
  { id: "enforcement", label: "Our right to act" },
  { id: "liability", label: "Our responsibility" },
  { id: "ending", label: "Ending your account" },
  { id: "changes", label: "Changes and law" },
  { id: "contact", label: "Contact us" },
];
---

<Page
  title="Terms and Conditions"
  description="The rules for using NyasaBuy: accounts, buying and selling, payments and fees, delivery, disputes and refunds, and what we expect from everyone."
>
  <LegalHeader
    title="Terms and Conditions"
    intro="The rules for buying and selling on NyasaBuy. Please read them. By creating an account or using the app you agree to them."
    updated="22 November 2026"
  />
  <GuideNav items={sections} />

  <article class="guide">
    <section id="summary">
      <Callout title="The short version" tone="safety">
        <ul>
          <li>You must be 18 or older, and give true information.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Only payments made inside the app are protected.</strong> Never
            pay a seller outside the app.
          </li>
          <li>
            Sellers must describe items honestly, only list what they have, and
            deliver what they sold.
          </li>
          <li>
            We keep a share of each sale. We hold the buyer's payment until the
            order is confirmed, then pay the seller.
          </li>
          <li>
            Be respectful. Scams, fake items, harassment and illegal goods get
            listings removed and accounts suspended.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Callout>
      <p>
        This summary is only a guide. The full terms below are what apply.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="about">
      <h2>1. About these terms</h2>
      <p>
        NyasaBuy ("<strong>NyasaBuy</strong>", "<strong>we</strong>",
        "<strong>us</strong>") runs an online marketplace in Malawi, through
        our mobile and web apps and this website, where people and businesses
        ("<strong>sellers</strong>") list items and services and other people
        ("<strong>buyers</strong>") can buy them. These Terms and Conditions
        ("<strong>Terms</strong>") are the agreement between you and NyasaBuy
        for everything you do on the platform.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains how we handle your
        personal information. It forms part of these Terms.
      </p>
      <h3>What NyasaBuy is, and is not</h3>
      <p>
        NyasaBuy is a platform that connects buyers and sellers and handles
        payment between them. <strong>We are not the seller of the items
        listed.</strong> The contract of sale is between the buyer and the
        seller. We do not own, inspect, store or deliver the items, and we do
        not guarantee that any listing, seller or buyer is accurate, honest or
        reliable. What we do provide is the marketplace, the chat, the secure
        payment flow, the order tracking, and a way to report and resolve
        problems.
      </p>
      <h3>Agreeing to these Terms</h3>
      <p>
        You agree to these Terms when you tick the box while creating your
        account, when you sign in for the first time with Google, or when you
        otherwise use NyasaBuy. If you do not agree, do not use the platform.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="accounts">
      <h2>2. Your account</h2>
      <h3>Who can use NyasaBuy</h3>
      <p>
        You must be at least 18 years old and able to make a binding agreement
        to open an account. If you register a business, you confirm you are
        allowed to act for it.
      </p>
      <h3>Giving us true information</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The details you give us (name, email, phone number, location,
          business details, payout details) must be true and kept up to date.
        </li>
        <li>You may have only one personal account.</li>
        <li>
          Do not pretend to be someone else, or use a name that copies another
          person, business or NyasaBuy itself. We may refuse or change names,
          usernames and business names that mislead, imitate the app, or break
          the rules in section 12. A business name must be unique on the
          platform.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Keeping your account safe</h3>
      <p>
        You are responsible for your password, your sign-in method (email or
        Google) and everything done through your account. Do not share your
        sign-in or one-time codes with anyone. Tell us straight away at the
        address in section 18 if you think someone else has used your account.
        We will never ask you for your password or a one-time code.
      </p>
      <h3>Verification</h3>
      <p>
        To sell, you must complete a seller application and give us the
        information we ask for. We may check it, ask for more, approve or
        decline an application, and withdraw approval later. Being approved is
        not an endorsement of you, your goods or your business.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="using">
      <h2>3. Using NyasaBuy</h2>
      <p>
        We give you a personal, limited, non-exclusive right to use the app
        and website for their intended purpose of buying and selling. In return
        you agree to use them lawfully and in line with these Terms. You must
        not:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          copy, scrape, reverse-engineer or attack the platform, or try to get
          into accounts or data that are not yours;
        </li>
        <li>
          use bots or automated tools to create accounts, send messages, make
          offers or place orders;
        </li>
        <li>
          interfere with how payments, ratings, search, featured listings or
          the online status work;
        </li>
        <li>
          use the platform to send spam, advertise other services, or collect
          other people's details.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We work to keep NyasaBuy available, but we do not promise it will
        always run without interruption or errors. We may update, change or
        pause parts of it, for example for maintenance or security.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="listings">
      <h2>4. Listings</h2>
      <p>
        A listing is an offer by a seller to sell something. When you create a
        listing you confirm that:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>you own the item or are allowed to sell it, and it is legal to sell;</li>
        <li>
          the title, photos, description, price, condition, location and
          quantity are accurate and not misleading;
        </li>
        <li>
          the photos are of the actual item (or a fair picture of it), and you
          have the right to use them;
        </li>
        <li>
          you really have the quantity shown, and you will keep it up to date
          so the same stock is not sold twice;
        </li>
        <li>
          the price is the full price in Malawi Kwacha (MWK), and you will not
          add hidden charges outside the app.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can edit a listing or withdraw it (take it off the marketplace) at
        any time. Withdrawing or editing a listing does not cancel orders that
        are already paid. A listing may be reserved for a short time while a
        buyer's payment is in progress. If it is not paid in time, it becomes
        available again. We may remove, hide or edit any listing that breaks
        these Terms, is reported, or that we believe may harm other users.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="buying">
      <h2>5. Buying</h2>
      <h3>How a purchase works</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>
          You find a listing and start a purchase. This opens a chat with the
          seller with a message already written for you, which you can edit
          before sending. You may agree a quantity, a price and a delivery time
          with the seller.
        </li>
        <li>
          The seller confirms that the item is available and accepts the terms
          you agreed. This confirmation is time-limited and shown in the chat.
        </li>
        <li>
          You then pay inside the app. Your payment is held by NyasaBuy and is
          not paid to the seller yet.
        </li>
        <li>
          The seller delivers. You confirm you received it, or report a
          problem. When the order is confirmed, we release the seller's money.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <h3>The cart</h3>
      <p>
        The cart is a place to hold items you are interested in. It does not
        reserve stock for you. When you check out, we send your request to
        each seller. You can continue to payment once the sellers have
        confirmed. Items that a seller has not confirmed, or whose confirmation
        has run out, cannot be paid for until they are confirmed again.
      </p>
      <h3>Your responsibilities as a buyer</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Read the listing and chat carefully before you pay.</li>
        <li>
          Pay only in the app, and only for the amount and quantity you agreed.
        </li>
        <li>
          Give a correct delivery location and be reachable so the seller can
          deliver.
        </li>
        <li>
          Confirm receipt, or report a problem, within the time shown on your
          order. Do not confirm an order you have not received.
        </li>
        <li>
          Do not place orders you do not intend to complete, or hold a seller's
          stock without paying.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="selling">
      <h2>6. Selling</h2>
      <h3>Your promises as a seller</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          You will only confirm a sale if you have the item, and you will
          deliver it by the delivery time you agreed with the buyer (at least
          2 days, so the buyer has a realistic time frame).
        </li>
        <li>
          The item will match the listing and what you agreed in the chat. You
          are responsible for its quality, legality and safety.
        </li>
        <li>
          You will pack and deliver it properly, and mark the order as
          delivered only when it has been handed over or sent.
        </li>
        <li>You will be responsive and polite to buyers.</li>
        <li>
          You are responsible for any tax, licence or permit that applies to
          your sales and your business.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h3>When you confirm a sale</h3>
      <p>
        When you accept a buyer's request or a negotiated price, you are
        agreeing to sell at that price and quantity. Please check it before you
        accept. A confirmation stays open for a limited time (shown in the
        chat). After that, the buyer needs to ask again.
      </p>
      <h3>Payout details</h3>
      <p>
        To withdraw your earnings you must give us a mobile money number or
        bank details that belong to you. If you change them, we may hold
        withdrawals for a short safety period (currently 24 hours) to protect
        you from account takeover. We may also ask you to confirm your
        identity before paying out.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="payments">
      <h2>7. Payments, fees and payouts</h2>
      <h3>Paying in the app</h3>
      <p>
        Payments are made in Malawi Kwacha through our payment partner
        (currently PayChangu), using Airtel Money, TNM Mpamba or a bank card.
        Your payment is processed by the payment partner and the mobile money
        or card provider, who have their own terms. We do not see or store your
        full card number or mobile money PIN.
      </p>
      <Callout title="Only payments in the app are protected" tone="safety">
        <p>
          If a buyer and seller agree to pay by Airtel Money, TNM Mpamba, bank
          transfer, cash or any other way outside the app, <strong>NyasaBuy
          cannot protect that payment, cannot help recover it, and will not
          resolve disputes about it</strong>. Asking someone to pay outside the
          app breaks these Terms and may lead to suspension.
        </p>
      </Callout>
      <h3>How money is held and released</h3>
      <p>
        When a buyer pays, the money is held by us for the order. It is
        released to the seller once the order is confirmed by the buyer, or
        confirmed automatically at the end of the confirmation period (see
        section 9), unless there is a dispute. Money for an order in dispute
        stays held until the dispute is resolved.
      </p>
      <h3>Our fee</h3>
      <p>
        We keep a percentage of each completed sale as our fee (the
        "<strong>commission</strong>"). The current percentage is shown in the
        app and on your earnings, and we may change it. A change applies only
        to orders paid after the change. Payment processing costs are covered
        from our share, not deducted again from the seller's. Sellers see what
        they will earn from an order before they confirm it.
      </p>
      <h3>Withdrawals</h3>
      <p>
        Earnings from completed orders can be withdrawn to your payout number
        or account. There is a minimum withdrawal amount (currently MWK 1,000),
        shown in the app. Withdrawals are normally sent automatically, but may
        be delayed by the payment provider, by a safety hold, or by a review
        by us. We may hold or reverse a payout if we reasonably believe it is
        linked to fraud, a mistake, a chargeback, or a breach of these Terms.
      </p>
      <h3>Mistakes and failed payments</h3>
      <p>
        If you are charged but the order does not go through (for example the
        item was sold to someone else at the same moment, or the listing was
        no longer available), the payment is refunded to you. Contact us with
        your payment reference if you do not see an update within a reasonable
        time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="delivery">
      <h2>8. Delivery and confirmation</h2>
      <p>
        Sellers deliver items themselves or through a courier or transport of
        their choice, as agreed in the chat. NyasaBuy does not deliver and is
        not responsible for the courier, delays, or loss in transit. Delivery
        costs, if any, should be agreed and included in the price in the app.
      </p>
      <p>
        When the seller marks an order as delivered, the buyer is asked to
        confirm that they received it, or report a problem. The same options
        appear in the chat, so the buyer can act from there too.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="disputes">
      <h2>9. Problems, disputes and refunds</h2>
      <h3>How long you have to confirm</h3>
      <p>
        Each order has an expected arrival time based on what the seller
        agreed. After that, the buyer has a short extra period (currently 3
        days) to confirm or report a problem. If the buyer does nothing in that
        time, the order is completed automatically and the seller is paid. If
        the buyer says the item has not arrived yet, they can ask for more
        time a limited number of times. After that, the matter is treated as
        a dispute. This is so that a seller's money is not held indefinitely.
        We send reminders before the time runs out.
      </p>
      <h3>Reporting a problem</h3>
      <p>
        A buyer can report a problem with a paid order, for example: the item
        did not arrive, is not as described, is damaged or is not what was
        agreed. Please explain clearly and provide photos or evidence where you
        can. A report opens a dispute and the money for that order stays held.
      </p>
      <h3>How we decide</h3>
      <p>
        We look at the listing, the chat, the order history, photos and
        evidence both sides provide, and our records. We may ask both sides
        for more information. Our decision may be to release the money to the
        seller, refund the buyer in full or in part, or take other action. We
        aim to be fair, but our decision on how to handle the held money is
        final for the purpose of the platform. This does not take away your
        legal rights.
      </p>
      <h3>Refunds</h3>
      <p>
        Refunds go back to the buyer through the payment method or wallet they
        used where possible, after we have recorded them. They can take some
        time to arrive because of the mobile money or bank provider. Our fee
        is not charged on refunded orders. Refunds are not available for
        payments made outside the app.
      </p>
      <h3>Reporting people</h3>
      <p>
        From a chat you can report the other person, for example for trying to
        take the payment outside the app, harassment, scams or other
        behaviour. When you report a chat, our team can read the last few
        messages from that conversation and the details you give, to decide
        what to do.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="boosts">
      <h2>10. Featured listings (boosts)</h2>
      <p>
        A seller can pay a fee to have a listing shown in the featured section
        of the home page for a set number of days. The current price and
        number of days are shown before you pay. A boost is a promotion, not a
        guarantee of sales, views or position. There is a limit on how many
        listings one seller can boost at the same time.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Featured listings are shown in turn, so one is not always at the
          front.
        </li>
        <li>
          If you remove a boost early, or withdraw the listing, or it is
          removed for breaking these Terms, the fee is not refunded.
        </li>
        <li>
          If a boost you paid for cannot be started because of a fault on our
          side, we will refund it.
        </li>
        <li>
          We may also feature listings ourselves, free of charge, for
          example to highlight a good seller or a category.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="chat">
      <h2>11. Chat, reviews and conduct</h2>
      <p>
        The chat is for talking about items and orders. Be honest, polite and
        reasonable. Do not use threatening, abusive, hateful, sexual or
        discriminatory language. Do not send spam or unrelated adverts. You can
        edit a message you sent, but we keep the history so that we can
        understand a dispute.
      </p>
      <p>
        Chats are not end-to-end private from us. We keep them as a record of
        what was agreed and may review them where there is a report, a
        dispute, a safety concern, or a legal duty. We do not read chats for
        any other reason without good cause.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reviews and ratings must be honest and based on a real purchase. Do not
        offer or accept payment or favours for reviews, and do not post fake
        reviews about yourself or a competitor.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Online status.</strong> The app can show other users when you
        are online or when you were last online. You can turn this off in your
        privacy settings. If you do, you also will not see others' status.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="prohibited">
      <h2>12. What is not allowed</h2>
      <h3>Not allowed to be sold</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Anything illegal in Malawi, stolen goods, counterfeit or pirated
          goods, and items that infringe someone else's rights.
        </li>
        <li>
          Weapons and ammunition, illegal drugs and drug paraphernalia, and
          controlled medicines or medical products you are not licensed to sell.
        </li>
        <li>
          Human or animal body parts, protected wildlife and wildlife products,
          and anything involving the exploitation of people or animals.
        </li>
        <li>
          Fake documents, stolen or hacked accounts and data, and services that
          help others cheat or commit fraud.
        </li>
        <li>Adult sexual content, and anything that could harm children.</li>
        <li>
          Money, gift cards, mobile airtime and similar items that can be used
          to move money around outside the app, unless we have said they are
          allowed.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Not allowed in behaviour</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Asking or pushing anyone to pay outside the app, including by Airtel
          Money, TNM Mpamba, bank transfer or cash, or sharing payment details
          in the chat for that purpose.
        </li>
        <li>
          Taking a payment and not delivering, delivering something different
          from the listing, or any other scam.
        </li>
        <li>
          Misleading titles, photos, prices or descriptions, "bait" prices, or
          holding listings you cannot supply.
        </li>
        <li>
          Using a name, username, business name or logo that copies NyasaBuy,
          its staff, or another person or business, or that suggests you work
          for us.
        </li>
        <li>
          Creating more than one account to avoid a suspension, manipulate
          ratings, or hide from a dispute.
        </li>
        <li>Harassing, threatening or discriminating against anyone.</li>
        <li>
          Sharing someone else's private information without their permission.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="content">
      <h2>13. Your content</h2>
      <p>
        You keep ownership of what you post: listings, photos, descriptions,
        reviews, messages and profile details ("<strong>your content</strong>").
        By posting it you give NyasaBuy a free, worldwide, non-exclusive
        licence to host, store, display, copy, resize and share it as needed to
        run, secure and promote the platform. For example, to show your listing
        in search and the featured section, in a link you or others share, or
        in a notification. This licence ends when you delete the content or
        your account, except for copies we must keep (see the Privacy Policy
        and section 16), and content others have already shared or saved.
      </p>
      <p>
        You promise that your content is yours to post, does not break anyone
        else's rights or the law, and is not harmful. The NyasaBuy name, logo,
        app and website belong to us. These Terms do not give you any right to
        use them except to use the platform.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="enforcement">
      <h2>14. Our right to act</h2>
      <p>
        To keep the platform safe and fair, we may, at our discretion and
        sometimes without notice:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>remove, hide or edit listings, messages and reviews;</li>
        <li>limit what an account can do, or ask for more verification;</li>
        <li>hold payments or payouts while we investigate;</li>
        <li>suspend or close accounts, temporarily or permanently;</li>
        <li>
          refuse or cancel an order, and refund the buyer where money has been
          paid;
        </li>
        <li>
          share information with the police, regulators, or the payment
          providers where the law allows or requires it, or to protect people.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If we act on your account, we will normally tell you why, unless the
        law or safety stops us. If you think we made a mistake, contact us
        and we will review it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="liability">
      <h2>15. Our responsibility</h2>
      <p>
        We do our best to run a safe and reliable marketplace, but there are
        limits to what we can promise.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Between users.</strong> We are not a party to the sale between
          buyer and seller. We do not guarantee the quality, safety, legality or
          delivery of items, or the conduct of users. Any dealing between you
          and another user is at your own risk, within the protection the
          in-app payment and dispute process gives you.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>As is.</strong> The platform is provided "as is" and "as
          available". We do not promise it will always be available, free of
          errors, or free of harmful code.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Limit.</strong> As far as the law allows, we are not liable
          for losses that are indirect, or loss of profit, business, data or
          goodwill, or for losses caused by users, by networks and mobile money
          or bank providers, by events outside our control, or by payments made
          outside the app. Where we are responsible to you, our total liability
          for any claim is limited to the amount you paid us in fees for the
          order the claim relates to, or MWK 100,000 if higher.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>What does not change.</strong> Nothing in these Terms limits
          liability that cannot be limited by law, or any rights you have as a
          consumer under Malawi law.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You agree to compensate us for losses and costs we suffer because of
        your breach of these Terms, your content, or your unlawful use of the
        platform.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="ending">
      <h2>16. Ending your account</h2>
      <p>
        You can stop using NyasaBuy at any time, and you can delete your
        account from the app's settings. You cannot delete your account while
        you have a paid order still in progress, so that the other person is
        not left without their item or their money. Finish or resolve those
        first. Unpaid orders are cancelled.
      </p>
      <p>
        When an account is deleted, you can no longer sign in, and your
        listings are taken off the marketplace. Your name and contact details
        are removed from your profile and replaced with "Deleted user".
        Records that other people, the law, or our accounting rely on, such as
        orders, payments, reviews, disputes and the chats connected to them,
        are kept. The Privacy Policy explains how long.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may end or suspend your access under section 14. Sections that
        should reasonably survive (for example about payments already made,
        disputes, your content licence for records we must keep, liability and
        the law that applies) continue after your account ends.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="changes">
      <h2>17. Changes, notices and the law</h2>
      <h3>Changes to these Terms</h3>
      <p>
        We may change these Terms, for example when we add features or when
        the law changes. We will post the new Terms on this page with a new
        date and, for important changes, tell you in the app or by email. If
        you keep using NyasaBuy after the change takes effect, you accept the
        new Terms. If you do not agree, stop using the platform and delete your
        account.
      </p>
      <h3>Notices</h3>
      <p>
        We may contact you through the app, by notification, or at the email
        address on your account. Keep your contact details current.
      </p>
      <h3>Governing law and disputes with us</h3>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Malawi. If we
        cannot sort out a disagreement together first, the courts of Malawi
        have the right to decide it. Please contact us first, because most
        problems can be resolved quickly.
      </p>
      <h3>General</h3>
      <p>
        If part of these Terms is found to be unenforceable, the rest still
        applies. If we do not enforce a right straight away, we have not given
        it up. You may not transfer your rights under these Terms to anyone
        else. We may transfer ours as part of a sale or reorganisation of the
        business. These Terms and the Privacy Policy are the whole agreement
        between you and us about the platform.
